\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1\cf0 .Savior, again to Thy dear Name we raise
\par With one accord our parting hymn of praise;
\par We stand to bless thee ere our worship cease,
\par Then, lowly kneeling, Thy word of peace.
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Grant us Thy peace upon homeward way;
\par With thee began Thee shall end the day;
\par Guard thou the lips from sin, the hearts from shame,
\par That in this house have called upon thy name.
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Grant us Thy peace through this approaching night;
\par Turn Thou for us its darkness into light;
\par From harm and danger keep Thy children free,
\par For dark and light are both alike to Thee.
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj 
\par \pard\fi-270\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.   Grant us Thy peace throughout our earthly life,
\par Our balm in sorrow, and stay in strife;
\par Then, when thy voice shall bid our conflict cease,
\par Call us, O Lord, to Thine eternal peace.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

